# @last-edited: 2026-11-16 UTC+7.
# @title: _headers — the CSP and cache policy every path of the site answers with.
# @state: one policy per path; every page may prove and renew the session against Supabase Auth, and /harga also reaches its own origin (/api/region) so the visitor's IP can pick the plan group.
# @dependencies: none.

# WHY this file exists: Cloudflare Pages configures headers with this file, one block per path. One path per block: a comma-joined path line matches nothing on Cloudflare.
# WHY the hashes are not in this file: the prerendered pages ship React Router's inline hydration boot, and those hashes are a function of each page's own build bytes — the build rewrites the deployed copy (site/scripts/inline-script-hashes.ts) with one hash list per page, so this file stays stable while the policy stays closed: script-src 'self' plus exactly the hashes that page emitted, never 'unsafe-inline'.
# WHY per page and never one list for the site: CSP headers are enforced as an intersection, so a second header can only block more, and one union list outgrew Cloudflare's header ceiling — an overlong policy is dropped entirely, which is how the boot script got blocked and every page was left as static HTML.
# tests/site parses the build and fails on drift.

/
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; connect-src https://*.supabase.co; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), bluetooth=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

